CM_ BO_ 256 "Minimal reproduction of a big-endian (Motorola) rolling-counter decoding bug. RollingCounter is a 4-bit nibble starting mid-byte (bit 11) and must increment 0..14 each frame. All other signals mirror the exact bit layout of the original reported message (renamed/anonymized), so the DBC parses and packs the full 32-byte frame exactly as in the field.";
CM_ SG_ 256 ChecksumByte "Byte-aligned 8-bit checksum/status byte, used as a sanity check that basic decoding still works.";
CM_ SG_ 256 RollingCounter "Rolling counter. Occupies the low nibble of byte 1 (bits 11..8). Must be seen incrementing 0,1,2,...,14,0,1,... when replaying rolling_counter_repro.py.";
CM_ SG_ 256 StatusBits "Unrelated 2-bit signal kept to make sure neighbouring signals aren't disturbed by the fix.";
